1
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:34,976
=Love Actually S5 Extra Episode=

2
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:35,680
Shall we go?

3
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:40,040
Shall we go?

4
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:41,319
What are you doing?

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:42,799
I'm waiting for you.

6
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:44,119
Let's go then.

7
00:00:44,119 --> 00:00:44,520
Let's go.

8
00:00:47,159 --> 00:00:48,919
Are you always this good-looking?

9
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:52,159
I'll outwork you to death.

10
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:56,680
You look like you're about to attend

11
00:00:57,759 --> 00:01:00,400
some kind of fancy banquet.

12
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,360
A fancy banquet.

13
00:01:17,879 --> 00:01:18,959
This cozy setting.

14
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:28,680
Do you want this egg?

15
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:30,680
Don't you eat eggs?

16
00:01:31,239 --> 00:01:32,319
I thought you loved eggs.

17
00:01:35,319 --> 00:01:36,319
I've got two here.

18
00:01:36,319 --> 00:01:37,000
You can have one.

19
00:01:38,279 --> 00:01:39,319
Thanks.

20
00:01:39,319 --> 00:01:39,760
No problem.

21
00:01:46,559 --> 00:01:47,879
Actually,
when you were playing that day,

22
00:01:47,879 --> 00:01:48,360
I thought,

23
00:01:49,319 --> 00:01:50,160
"This guy is so handsome."

24
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:54,559
Actually, I wasn't at my best that day.

25
00:01:55,919 --> 00:01:57,040
I think you're very handsome.

26
00:01:57,040 --> 00:01:58,080
You played beautifully.

27
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:00,760
I'm speaking

28
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:01,800
from the bottom of my heart.

29
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:03,160
Why are you rolling your eyes?

30
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:03,760
Really.

31
00:02:04,239 --> 00:02:05,279
When I was looking at you,

32
00:02:05,279 --> 00:02:05,800
I thought,

33
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,120
"How is this guy so handsome?"

34
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:07,959
Bubbles were popping up behind you.

35
00:02:07,959 --> 00:02:09,320
There was a beam of light behind you.

36
00:02:09,320 --> 00:02:11,600
A beam of light was shining on you.

37
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:14,919
Don't get all shy on me now.

38
00:02:15,399 --> 00:02:16,360
I'm getting shy.

39
00:02:17,199 --> 00:02:18,199
You're getting shy?

40
00:02:18,199 --> 00:02:19,279
So this is what you look like
when you're shy?

41
00:02:21,839 --> 00:02:23,080
But right now, I really regret

42
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:25,119
why I didn't learn more things
back then.

43
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:27,720
You can start learning now.

44
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:29,679
What's there to regret?

45
00:02:30,839 --> 00:02:31,759
Learn a bit

46
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:33,559
about advertising, or something.

47
00:02:33,559 --> 00:02:35,296
(Speaking with hidden meaning)

48
00:02:35,808 --> 00:02:37,600
(Advertising company owner)

49
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:41,039
Aren't you about to fire someone?

50
00:02:41,039 --> 00:02:42,016
(Starting to talk nonsense)

51
00:02:45,374 --> 00:02:46,240
(Just imagining it is lovely)

52
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:46,679
Come on then.

53
00:02:46,679 --> 00:02:47,360
Well, I have to think

54
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,839
about what monthly salary
I should offer you.

55
00:02:48,839 --> 00:02:50,479
(Direct Boss Chat)

56
00:02:50,479 --> 00:02:52,360
Do you always require

57
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:53,919
that job seekers have this kind

58
00:02:53,919 --> 00:02:54,639
of experience,

59
00:02:54,639 --> 00:02:57,360
like in this line of work?

60
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:58,080
For now,

61
00:02:58,080 --> 00:02:59,800
I need someone with experience.

62
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:01,080
Understood.

63
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:02,919
So I'd just be a security guard then.

64
00:03:02,919 --> 00:03:04,080
You could be a nanny.

65
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:05,679
You could be a personal assistant.

66
00:03:06,919 --> 00:03:08,199
I also have a dream.

67
00:03:08,199 --> 00:03:10,320
To be someone's driver.

68
00:03:11,559 --> 00:03:12,759
I'll bring my own white gloves.

69
00:03:15,119 --> 00:03:16,039
I'll drive for you.

70
00:03:17,679 --> 00:03:19,479
You are hinting at, right?

71
00:03:19,919 --> 00:03:20,919
You're giving me a little hint.

72
00:03:21,720 --> 00:03:23,360
I just wanted to experience

73
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:24,880
what it feels like to drive the car.

74
00:03:25,399 --> 00:03:26,279
So what you're saying is,

75
00:03:26,279 --> 00:03:27,479
I still have to work harder.

76
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:30,479
Have you ever thought

77
00:03:30,479 --> 00:03:32,000
about what kind of house
you want to live in?

78
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:35,639
I don't have many requirements
for a house.

79
00:03:35,639 --> 00:03:36,919
It just needs to be quiet.

80
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:39,559
You're living
in the city center now, right?

81
00:03:39,559 --> 00:03:40,440
I guess so.

82
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:41,399
So you don't really mind.

83
00:03:42,639 --> 00:03:44,039
Because it's close to my office.

84
00:03:44,039 --> 00:03:45,360
If I have to spend an hour

85
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:46,479
or two getting home after work,

86
00:03:46,479 --> 00:03:47,839
I would be devastated.

87
00:03:48,639 --> 00:03:49,839
Then we're completely opposite.

88
00:03:50,679 --> 00:03:52,919
Every day, going into the city,

89
00:03:52,919 --> 00:03:54,800
driving takes me almost an hour.

90
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,240
When I was in a bad mood in the past,

91
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:57,880
I would drive alone,

92
00:03:57,880 --> 00:03:58,839
sing loudly,

93
00:03:58,839 --> 00:03:59,919
and cry my eyes out in the car.

94
00:04:04,119 --> 00:04:05,320
Then, when I got home,

95
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:06,520
I'd wipe my tears and go upstairs.

96
00:04:08,399 --> 00:04:10,000
It's because, inside the car,

97
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:10,800
you feel like

98
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:12,559
it's completely your own space.

99
00:04:12,559 --> 00:04:13,119
It's a private space of your own.

100
00:04:13,119 --> 00:04:13,559
Right.

101
00:04:13,960 --> 00:04:14,880
You can do whatever you want.

102
00:04:16,119 --> 00:04:16,920
I actually really...

103
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:17,519
Even if,

104
00:04:17,519 --> 00:04:19,119
okay, I'm really tired today,

105
00:04:19,839 --> 00:04:21,640
I still want to go home every day.

106
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:22,480
Okay, maybe it takes me over an hour

107
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:23,600
to drive home,

108
00:04:24,359 --> 00:04:25,959
but for me, I feel that this hour

109
00:04:25,959 --> 00:04:27,399
is a time to relax.

110
00:04:28,119 --> 00:04:30,119
I just turn on some music,

111
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:33,280
and I feel that's already very relaxing.

112
00:04:39,119 --> 00:04:40,320
Why am I suddenly hungry?

113
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:41,519
Eat.

114
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:43,399
You didn't eat enough at lunch,
for sure.

115
00:04:43,959 --> 00:04:46,040
What are we going to eat
back at the house tonight?

116
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:48,720
There's your delivery.

117
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:50,920
Then maybe I should
order something else.

118
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:52,720
Or I could make something.

119
00:04:53,640 --> 00:04:54,399
You haven't tried

120
00:04:54,399 --> 00:04:55,239
anything I've made, have you?

121
00:04:55,679 --> 00:04:56,640
Nothing at all.

122
00:04:56,640 --> 00:04:57,799
Except for toast.

123
00:05:00,799 --> 00:05:01,320
I saw

124
00:05:02,079 --> 00:05:02,959
that everyone else can cook,

125
00:05:02,959 --> 00:05:03,720
so I won't bother.

126
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:07,040
There's no room for me to shine.

127
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:08,119
Then, shall we go grocery shopping?

128
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:09,880
If you want to eat something I make,

129
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:10,880
we can go to the supermarket.

130
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:11,760
Let's go to the supermarket.

131
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:18,200
That voice sounds so familiar.

132
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:18,720
Let's go.

133
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:19,160
Go.

134
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:28,160
My heel got stuck again.

135
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:28,679
Oh, no.

136
00:05:29,880 --> 00:05:30,600
I got it.

137
00:05:34,399 --> 00:05:34,920
Oh, dear.

138
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:38,119
Can you move it?

139
00:05:41,679 --> 00:05:42,600
Oh, no.

140
00:05:45,839 --> 00:05:46,519
I'm in trouble.

141
00:05:48,959 --> 00:05:49,839
I got it.

142
00:05:50,279 --> 00:05:50,720
What's wrong?

143
00:05:52,799 --> 00:05:53,040
Like this.

144
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:55,279
It's out.

145
00:05:55,279 --> 00:05:55,920
Then let's go down.

146
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:06,799
You look so sleepy-eyed.

147
00:06:06,799 --> 00:06:07,720
So sleepy.

148
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:09,720
I was so tired I fell asleep.

149
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:13,679
My hair is doing a chicken lady again.

150
00:06:13,679 --> 00:06:14,559
Chicken lady.

151
00:06:16,679 --> 00:06:18,200
Actually, it looks pretty good.

152
00:06:19,399 --> 00:06:21,440
Let's see what we need.

153
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:23,880
Zucchini and carrots.

154
00:06:23,880 --> 00:06:24,760
I'll carry them.

155
00:06:26,399 --> 00:06:27,200
Two zucchinis

156
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:28,600
and one carrot is enough.

157
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:29,040
That's enough.

158
00:06:30,440 --> 00:06:32,399
We don't need scallions today, right?

159
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:34,279
Is there any lemon left?

160
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:36,239
No.

161
00:06:36,239 --> 00:06:37,079
Then buy some lemons.

162
00:06:37,079 --> 00:06:38,040
Let's buy some lemons.

163
00:06:39,480 --> 00:06:39,880
Thanks.

164
00:06:41,399 --> 00:06:41,799
And

165
00:06:43,079 --> 00:06:44,200
go get the salmon.

166
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:44,640
Okay.

167
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:46,279
May I ask,

168
00:06:46,279 --> 00:06:47,720
usually, for salmon,

169
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:48,679
what kind of fish should be used?

170
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:51,320
No, what fish is used for pickled fish?

171
00:06:52,799 --> 00:06:54,000
What fish is used for pickled fish?

172
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,000
For pickled fish, well,

173
00:06:55,640 --> 00:06:56,320
there are a few kinds.

174
00:06:56,320 --> 00:06:57,279
This fathead fish.

175
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:58,679
Do you have snakehead?

176
00:06:58,679 --> 00:06:59,359
Snakehead.

177
00:06:59,880 --> 00:07:00,760
We have snakehead.

178
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:01,839
Then I'll take one snakehead, please.

179
00:07:01,839 --> 00:07:02,399
Thank you.

180
00:07:03,279 --> 00:07:03,640
Weigh it.

181
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:05,239
Okay, that's fine. Thank you.

182
00:07:05,239 --> 00:07:05,640
No problem.

183
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:07,200
Let's go.

184
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:07,559
Let's go.

185
00:07:07,959 --> 00:07:08,920
Shopping done.

186
00:07:12,679 --> 00:07:13,279
Slow down a bit.

187
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:15,399
Go.

188
00:07:17,079 --> 00:07:19,480
It reminds me of the story
of the Little Mermaid.

189
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:20,040
What mermaid?

190
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:21,519
To have feet

191
00:07:21,519 --> 00:07:22,760
for going on land,

192
00:07:22,760 --> 00:07:23,839
the mermaid gave up her voice.

193
00:07:23,839 --> 00:07:24,920
She couldn't speak anymore.

194
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:28,760
And her feet hurt with every step.

195
00:07:29,640 --> 00:07:31,519
And the tears she shed,

196
00:07:31,519 --> 00:07:33,160
those pearls, could be sold for money.

197
00:07:34,239 --> 00:07:35,000
(Pearls)
I'll catch them.

198
00:07:36,519 --> 00:07:37,640
Let me get rich.

199
00:07:44,160 --> 00:07:45,079
Dong.

200
00:07:45,880 --> 00:07:46,519
The delivery is here.

201
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:50,720
Yeah, and Xuan is going
to make some food.

202
00:07:54,119 --> 00:07:55,119
Come on. Tell me how...

203
00:07:55,119 --> 00:07:56,320
Cut into strips, right?

204
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:56,920
I can cut.

205
00:07:56,920 --> 00:07:57,519
Come on. Let me do it.

206
00:07:57,519 --> 00:07:58,799
The knife is really dull.

207
00:07:58,799 --> 00:07:59,119
I'll do it.

208
00:07:59,519 --> 00:08:00,200
Let me try

209
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:01,399
if this knife is better.

210
00:08:02,679 --> 00:08:03,279
I'll give it a try.

211
00:08:03,279 --> 00:08:03,640
Let me try.

212
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:04,040
I'll do it.

213
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:05,720
You go do something else.

214
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:06,480
I'll help you

215
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:08,160
finish cutting this,
and then you take over.

216
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:11,559
Even your back teeth are straining.

217
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:15,000
Was it fun today?

218
00:08:15,519 --> 00:08:16,720
Yes.

219
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:17,399
What did you do?

220
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:20,000
I'm not telling you.

221
00:08:21,119 --> 00:08:22,079
Give me a hint.

222
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:30,920
So hilarious.

223
00:08:31,456 --> 00:08:32,672
Sigh.

224
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:36,576
(Washing dishes is tough,
a handsome guy sighs)

225
00:08:38,239 --> 00:08:40,280
He's sighing there,
while washing dishes.

226
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:41,719
Just like me a few days ago.

227
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:43,039
While washing, I just...

228
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:46,200
Wentao says, "I couldn't take it.
Get someone else here."

229
00:08:46,200 --> 00:08:47,840
He just says,
"How can they make such a mess."

230
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:48,679
Three people take turns to do it.

231
00:08:49,479 --> 00:08:50,679
It's okay. I'll do it later.

232
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:52,119
No need. It's fine.

233
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:58,559
Xiaowen's image in our hearts

234
00:08:58,559 --> 00:08:59,400
has become so much greater.

235
00:09:00,239 --> 00:09:00,840
Why?

236
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:02,039
Because he cooks?

237
00:09:02,039 --> 00:09:03,640
He can cook and wash dishes,

238
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:04,400
and he's handsome.

239
00:09:04,704 --> 00:09:05,568
(Happy)

240
00:09:05,568 --> 00:09:06,280
(Unhappy)

241
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:07,679
I can also cook and wash dishes.

242
00:09:07,679 --> 00:09:08,559
Why don't you compliment me?

243
00:09:08,559 --> 00:09:09,280
I've always said

244
00:09:09,280 --> 00:09:10,599
(So easy to please)
that you're the greatest woman.

245
00:09:13,359 --> 00:09:14,840
Leave it. That's enough.

246
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:16,440
I'll wash after we eat.

247
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,440
No, you cooked.

248
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:19,280
So you can't wash them.

249
00:09:20,479 --> 00:09:20,960
I can.

250
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:21,880
Look at Wentao.

251
00:09:22,679 --> 00:09:24,239
Life warms up

252
00:09:24,239 --> 00:09:25,080
in these details.

253
00:09:26,239 --> 00:09:27,760
The general rule is

254
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:29,679
the person who cooks
shouldn't wash dishes.

255
00:09:29,679 --> 00:09:30,119
Right.

256
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:32,440
Because cooking is hard work.

257
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:33,280
Prepping ingredients, right?

258
00:09:34,239 --> 00:09:35,359
This is

259
00:09:36,159 --> 00:09:36,919
thousand-layer tofu.

260
00:09:37,760 --> 00:09:38,039
Incredible.

261
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:40,440
Hot.

262
00:09:40,440 --> 00:09:40,760
Blow on it.

263
00:09:48,679 --> 00:09:49,039
Okay.

264
00:09:50,919 --> 00:09:51,960
It's so good.

265
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:53,840
If you eat this, you'll live to 99.

266
00:09:55,880 --> 00:09:57,479
How is this dish so beautiful?

267
00:09:57,479 --> 00:09:58,599
So beautiful.

268
00:09:58,599 --> 00:10:00,280
Dong really knows how to live.

269
00:10:00,280 --> 00:10:01,799
Dong is still the best.

270
00:10:01,799 --> 00:10:03,000
Even an old Ferrari is still a Ferrari.

271
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:03,400
Yeah!

272
00:10:06,679 --> 00:10:07,799
So good.

273
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:09,239
Let's take another group photo

274
00:10:09,239 --> 00:10:10,559
to celebrate our hard work.

275
00:10:10,559 --> 00:10:12,280
One meal down, one less to go,
my friends.

276
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:13,479
No, it won't.

277
00:10:13,479 --> 00:10:14,400
We can still eat

278
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:15,280
in other places.

279
00:10:16,039 --> 00:10:16,280
Right.

280
00:10:16,280 --> 00:10:16,799
We'll take turns.

281
00:10:16,799 --> 00:10:17,640
We two can eat anytime.

282
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:19,239
We'll take turns dining
at each other's homes.

283
00:10:19,239 --> 00:10:19,919
Exactly.

284
00:10:21,520 --> 00:10:22,039
Perfect.

285
00:10:22,039 --> 00:10:22,479
Have a seat.

286
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:24,119
Thanks.

287
00:10:24,840 --> 00:10:26,119
There's so much delicious food.

288
00:10:26,119 --> 00:10:27,159
